From dbbf8e0b09023662ae14a6b0707761058b65e381 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:39:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move works archive to MongoDB (via Mongoose), add /admin
 panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The works/conversions archive no longer lives in a static src/data/projects.ts
array — it's now a MongoDB collection, modeled with Mongoose (src/models/Work.ts,
src/lib/works.ts) so it can grow without a code change or redeploy. Pagination,
the homepage teaser and project detail pages read from Mongo; page size and
page-token logic are unchanged, just driven by real data instead of a
build-time array padded with placeholder cards.

Adds a small password-protected /admin panel (single shared password, no
user accounts — see src/lib/session.ts) where a non-developer can add,
edit, delete and reorder works: maker/article/scale, title/type/works-list/
summary per language (uk/en/de), and 3 photos per work (drag-and-drop
upload, stored in MongoDB via GridFS and served from /api/images/[id]).
URL slugs are generated automatically so the admin never has to think
about one.

Since content now changes at runtime, the site is no longer a static
export: next.config.ts drops output: 'export', and every page that reads
works data is marked force-dynamic. scripts/seed.mjs migrates the
original 6 conversions into a fresh database (safe to re-run).

See .env.example for the new required environment variables
(MONGODB_URI, ADMIN_PASSWORD, SESSION_SECRET) and README.md for the
updated deploy steps.

